issue_body:
## Context

We need to plus this new system in all the places that compute a product price, we identify to `Product::getPriceStatic` is the main endpoint that is always called. So the new system should be placed in this method, but this only handles the retro-compatibility part, the purpose, in fine, is to stop calling this method. To do that we need to identify all the places where we'll have to integrate the new system.

## A bit of code

### `getPriceStatic`

```php
public static function getPriceStatic(...)
{
    if (fetureFlagIsOn) {
       $productCalculator = $this->getContainer()->get(...);
       $priceDTO = $productCalculator->computePrice();

       // based on the 17 provided parameters we need to return the appropriate float value
       return $floatValue;
    }
}
```

### Callers of the `getPriceStatic`

Before

```php
class ProductController {
    public assignAttributesGroups()
    {
         ...
         $price = Product::getPriceStatic();
         ...
    }
}
```

After

```php
class ProductController {
    public assignAttributesGroups()
    {
         ...
         if (featureFlagIsOn) {
             $productCalculator = $this->getContainer()->get(...);
             $priceDTO = $productCalculator->computePrice();
             // based on the 17 provided parameters we need to return the appropriate float value
             $price = $floatValue;
         } else {
             $price = Product::getPriceStatic();
         }
         ...
    }
}
```

This replacement will have to be done **everywhere** the `getPriceStatic` (and maybe `priceCalculation`) method is called.

## Tasks

**/!\ Please read all the tasks to have the big picture in mind**

- [x] Integrate the calculator in `getPriceStatic`
- [x] List all the endpoints where `getPriceStatic` is called to have an exhaustive list of the code that will have to be adapted for the `ProductCalculator`
- [x] Integrate the `ProductCalculator` in place of `getPriceStatic` in at least one of these places
  - [ ] Use the product page display as the example
  - [ ] So probably in the `ProductController` class
  - [ ] But maybe it's actually done by the `ProductLazyArray`
  - [ ] But maybe not! So your mission, if you accept it, is to track where it's done
- [ ] Rough idea to improve DX, maybe we should have a `ProductCalculatorFactory` than handles the switch of the FF and building the service internally
